{
  "file": "crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs",
  "item": "impl[StoredGraph/NodeContents]/fn[format_node_content]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This storage-only domain verifies output decoding without reading or\n presenting node contents. A formatter call would be an unwanted graph\n access. Agent fixtures exercise formatting separately."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs#impl[StoredGraph/NodeContents]/fn[format_node_content]` is a valid coverage exception.\n\n- **Form:** The citation sits on an explicit function with a body. Its explanation is in fenced `:::{cite}` commentary, which the built-in text accepts. The explanation is substantive. It says the function is a guard that must never run, because the storage-only domain neither reads nor presents node contents.\n- **Fit with the source:** The function body is `panic!(\"storage operations must not format graph contents\")`, so it exists only to satisfy the `NodeContents` trait and fails loudly if called.\n  - `StoredGraph` is used only in the storage tests `malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors` and `consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path`, and as the graph for `StoredReview`. None of these format contents.\n  - `format_node_content` is called only by the agent dispatch in `src/agent/tools.rs` and by `Ask::execute` in `src/procedure.rs`. Neither is used with `StoredGraph`.\n  - The commentary's claim that other fixtures cover formatting is supported by the other fixtures that implement `format_node_content`: `tests/agent.rs` `Memory` and `tests/validation.rs` `Memory`.\n- **Why zero execution is acceptable:** Executing the function would be a test failure, so unexecuted is its correct state.",
